; ======================================================================
;  flash_layout.pico2 - where the PDP-11 keeps things in a board's flash.
;  THE ONE PLACE: the firmware (disk.pico2, psram_pdp11.pico2), the pack
;  installer (packinstall.pico2) and the host tools (tools/flash_layout.py,
;  which reads THIS file) all take the addresses from here. Offsets are
;  from the start of the flash; add $10000000 for the address.
;
;  THE RULE, for every RP2350 board the project builds for:
;      $000000 - $04DFFF program; $04E000 - $04EFFF E10 reserved
;      $04F000 output settings; $050000 - $1FFFFF unused gap
;      $200000 - $23FFFF   NEVER USED BY THE PDP-11. On a board with a
;                          radio this is where the radio chip's firmware
;                          is kept (the compiler's RP2350/Lib/cyw43.pico2
;                          reads it from $10200000, about 227 KB), and it
;                          must survive a pack being installed. A board
;                          without a radio leaves it empty, so one image
;                          family and one rule serve them all.
;      $240000 - ...       the packs: RK0 first, then RK1 where the flash
;                          is big enough for both.
;  A pack region is one 4 KB header sector and then 512-byte blocks
;  (disk.pico2, THE FLASH PACK).
;      RK0  $240000   4872 blocks dense = $262000 bytes, ends $4A1FFF
;      RK1  $4C0000   4000 blocks dense = $1F5000 bytes, ends $6B4FFF
;      or the RP03's pack (rp11.pico2), mapped, up to the store
;      the store: the top #FL_STORE_SIZE (1 MB) of the flash on the PSRAM
;           boards, where saves put the packs' changes (store.pico2)
;  What each board holds:
;      16 MB (Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 / 2 W)   RK0 and RK1
;       8 MB (Adafruit Feather RP2350)      RK0 and RK1
;       4 MB (Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W)        RK0 only, 1.75 MB of it: a
;                                           pack is stored MAPPED (only
;                                           the blocks in use) when it
;                                           does not fit dense
;  The installer refuses any region that starts below #FL_PACKS or
;  touches #FL_RADIO_LO to #FL_RADIO_HI, on every board; tools/rk_image.py
;  and tools/pack_install.py refuse the same before anything is sent.
;
;  Constants, and the regions below (FlashRegion: the IDE's Board Storage panel reads them;
;  they emit nothing): this file may be included by any program for an RP2350 board.
; ======================================================================
; The A2 BOOTSEL E10 write is confined to this otherwise unused sector.
; Never put it at flash end: the PSRAM saved-change store occupies that space.
#FL_E10 = $04E000
#FL_E10_SIZE = $001000
FlashRegion "UF2 E10 workaround", #FL_E10, #FL_E10_SIZE, "reserved"
#FL_RADIO_LO = $200000       ; the radio firmware's region: first byte
#FL_RADIO_HI = $240000       ; ... and the first byte after it
#FL_PACKS    = $240000       ; no pack region starts below this
#FL_RK0      = $240000       ; RK0's pack
#FL_RK1      = $4C0000       ; RK1's pack (boards with 8 MB of flash or more)
#FL_STORE_SIZE = $100000     ; the PSRAM boards' store of saved changes: the top 1 MB of the flash (store.pico2)

; THE SAME LAYOUT, AS NAMED REGIONS (FlashRegion): the PureMetal Forge IDE's Board Storage panel
; shows the flash map from these, writes a pack into its region and reads one back, and the
; build refuses a firmware that grows into one. They emit nothing into the firmware. By the
; board the program is built for (#PM_FLASH_BYTES, its board file's "FlashBytes").
#FL_RADIO_SIZE = #FL_RADIO_HI - #FL_RADIO_LO
FlashRegion "radio firmware", #FL_RADIO_LO, #FL_RADIO_SIZE, "reserved"
CompilerIf #PM_FLASH_BYTES >= $800000
#FL_STORE_AT = #PM_FLASH_BYTES - #FL_STORE_SIZE
FlashRegion "RK0", #FL_RK0, $262000, "rk05"                          ; 4872 blocks dense, ends $4A1FFF
FlashRegion "RK1", #FL_RK1, $1F5000, "rk05"                          ; 4000 blocks dense, ends $6B4FFF
FlashRegion "store", #FL_STORE_AT, #FL_STORE_SIZE, "reserved"        ; saved changes (store.pico2)
CompilerElse
#FL_RK0_SIZE = #PM_FLASH_BYTES - #FL_RK0
FlashRegion "RK0", #FL_RK0, #FL_RK0_SIZE, "rk05"                     ; 1.75 MB: a pack is stored mapped
CompilerEndIf
